-# Server changes iOS needs (not applied, not deployed)
+# Retired Apple verifier
 
-The iOS app reuses the account service (`aurora-android/server`, Cloudflare Worker + D1, Firebase project `aurora-24aa9`) unchanged for
-sign-in, sync, devices, the Free allowance and deletion, including the per-phone allowance and device proof from `fe78039`.
+The former apple-verify.js patch is insecure and must not be deployed. Its executable entry point and tests have been removed.
 
-## Test it
-
-`server-patches/run-tests.sh` copies the server to a temp folder, adds the patch and the route, and runs the server's own tests plus
-`test/apple.test.js`. Nothing in the Android repository changes and nothing is deployed. It covers: Apple-confirmed purchase, the API token,
-forged transactions, ownership, `appAccountToken`, idempotency, every status, refunds, sandbox rules, Apple down or unreadable, wrong app or
-product, bad input, sign-in, cross-platform Plus and seats. Apple itself is faked at the fetch boundary, so **this doesn't prove Apple's real responses**.
-
-## Apply it, when you approve
-
-1. **`/v1/verify/apple`**: paste `apple-verify.js` into `server/src/worker.js` above `ROUTES` and add `'/v1/verify/apple': verifyApple,`.
-   Secrets with `wrangler secret put`: `APPLE_ISSUER_ID`, `APPLE_KEY_ID`, `APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY` (base64 PKCS#8 of the .p8 key), `APPLE_BUNDLE_ID`
-   (`com.aagamjain.Aurora`). No D1 migration: purchases go in `purchases`, keyed by `sha256("apple:" + originalTransactionId)`.
-2. **`APPLE_ALLOW_SANDBOX=1`** while App Review and TestFlight use the sandbox. With it on, sandbox purchases grant Plus on production accounts.
-   Your decision when to turn it off.
-3. **Universal link for email sign-in**: put this in `auth-hosting/.well-known/apple-app-site-association`, say "your phone" instead of "your
-   Android phone" in `index.html`, and add Associated Domains (`applinks:aurora-24aa9.firebaseapp.com`). Until then iOS users paste the link.
-
-```json
-{ "applinks": { "details": [ { "appIDs": ["BZZV9Z8W24.com.aagamjain.Aurora"], "components": [ { "/": "/finish-sign-in*" }, { "/": "/__/auth/links*" } ] } ] } }
-```
-
-4. **Firebase console**: enable Apple sign-in; add an iOS app and put its OAuth client ID in `Config/Secrets.xcconfig` as `AURORA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`,
-   with the reversed form as a URL scheme.
-
-## What the review changed
-
-The earlier patch took the first transaction Apple returned rather than the one asked about, never checked the bundle or the account stamp, let sandbox
-purchases through always, could crash on an unreadable answer, and passed non-numeric ids to Apple. All fixed and tested.
-
-## Still open
-
-- **App Store Server Notifications V2** (renewals, refunds): not written. State refreshes on app start and Restore, as Android before RTDN. A refund only takes effect at the next check.
-- **Moving a subscription between accounts**: no App Store route. iOS says "sign in to that account" instead.
-- **Sign in with Apple token revocation on account deletion** (App Store Guideline 5.1.1(v)): not implemented. Needs a server route and the Apple key.
-- `privacy-policy.html` describes Google Play and Play Integrity only. It needs an App Store and Screen Time section before release.
